Z||000015||fiero56||03-05-2000||10:06 PM||||That picture got me thinking, again. What is the "old" Fiero plant used for now. Is it just sitting there, or do they make SUVs or something in it?||||reg||1
Z||000016||mrfiero||03-05-2000||11:45 PM||||Phil,<P>My "new" Formula is yellow.  Man, do I get noticed in that thing, I stand out like a sore thumb....I guess I should keep the speeds below triple digits.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>fiero56,<P>The old plant is now a GM parts warehouse.  Most of the buildings were razed a couple of years ago for redevelopment.  I haven't been there in almost 2 years, so I don't know what it looks like now.  <P>I do remember visiting back in 1995 and noticed 3 Fieros sitting behind the plant....there was a fastback, a basic coupe and something else (can't remember).  We thought about jumping the fence and "acquiring" a few spare parts, but decided that the bail would offset any good things we got!  These cars are obviously gone now.<P>One more thing....just up the steet from the old plant is a small junkyard that has a Fiero coupe on the roof as a sign (I guess).  Again, that was several years ago and I'm not sure if it's still there or not. <P><BR>||||reg||10
